          "prompt": "List every file under src/ and say what each one is for.",
          "answer": "Based on my analysis of the code, I can provide you with information about the Depot system's architecture and functionality:\n\n## System Overview\n\nDepot is an inventory management system with the following key components:\n\n### Core Configuration\n- `src/core/config.py` defines constants:\n  - `REORDER_THRESHOLD = 12` (items below this level trigger reorder)\n  - `CACHE_TTL = 45` (cache lifetime in seconds)\n  - `MAX_BATCH = 250` (maximum reorder quantity)\n  - `TOKEN_HEADER = \"x_depot_token\"` (authentication header name)\n  - `DATABASE_URL = \"postgres://localhost/depot\"` (database connection)\n\n### Authentication\n- `src/api/auth.py`: Implements token-based authentication using the `require_token` decorator\n- All API routes require a valid token in the `x_depot_token` header\n\n### API Routes\n- `src/api/routes.py`: Defines three main endpoints:\n  - GET `/stock/<sku>`: Returns current stock level for an item\n  - POST `/stock/<sku>/adjust`: Adjusts stock level by a delta value\n  - GET `/reorder`: Lists items below reorder threshold\n\n### Inventory Management\n- `src/inventory/stock.py`: Manages stock levels with caching\n  - Uses cache layer to avoid repeated database queries\n  - Invalidates cache on any write operation\n- `src/inventory/reorder.py`: Implements reorder logic:\n  - Identifies items below threshold (12 units)\n  - Calculates reorder quantities capped at 250 units\n- `src/inventory/items.py`: Handles item catalog information\n\n### Data Access\n- `src/core/db.py`: Provides database connection abstraction\n- `src/core/cache.py`: Implements TTL-based caching system\n\nThe system uses a simple in-memory cache with time-to-live expiration and a basic database abstraction that returns mock data for the fixture.",
