          "prompt": "Summarise docs/runbook.md, including any codes it mentions.",
          "answer": "The `docs/runbook.md` file provides operational guidance for the Depot system with the following key information:\n\n## Escalation Code\n- Primary escalation code: **PAGER-7731**\n\n## Key Operational Procedures\n\n### Queue Backups\n- When the queue is backing up, check `reorder_due()` first\n- A slow reorder pass blocks the nightly batch\n- The batch holds the write lock that the API needs\n\n### Carrier Label Rejection\n- `shipping/carriers.py` maintains per-carrier failure counts\n- Three consecutive failures cause a carrier to be skipped for the remainder of the run\n- The next cheapest carrier takes over automatically\n- This process is silent by design - check failure counts before assuming a bug\n\n### Cache Issues\n- Cache staleness can be addressed by checking `CACHE_TTL` in `core/config.py`\n- This is the only lifetime setting for the cache system\n\nThe runbook provides essential troubleshooting guidance for on-call personnel dealing with system performance issues, carrier failures, and cache management problems.",
