          "prompt": "What does src/shipping/carriers.py do?",
          "answer": "The `src/shipping/carriers.py` file implements a carrier selection and failure tracking system for the Depot shipping process. Here's what it does:\n\n## Carrier Information\n- Defines three carriers with their pricing structures:\n  - \"ravenpost\": $4.20 base + $0.85 per kg\n  - \"tortoise\": $2.10 base + $1.60 per kg  \n  - \"kestrel\": $6.00 base + $0.40 per kg\n\n## Failure Tracking System\n- Maintains a failure count for each carrier in `_failures` dictionary\n- Tracks how many consecutive failures each carrier has experienced\n\n## Key Functions\n\n### `quote(name, weight_kg)`\n- Calculates the shipping cost for a given carrier and package weight\n- Returns the rounded total cost\n\n### `cheapest(weight_kg)`\n- Determines the cheapest available carrier for a given weight\n- Excludes carriers with 3 or more consecutive failures\n- Uses the `quote()` function to compare costs\n\n### `record_failure(name)`\n- Records a failed label for a carrier (increments failure count)\n- Returns the updated failure count\n\n## Failure Handling\nThe system automatically skips carriers that have experienced 3 consecutive failed labels, ensuring that shipping operations continue with reliable carriers while maintaining cost efficiency through dynamic pricing comparisons.",
